  "original_hypotheses": [
    "N is a positive level. g,h are any genuine integral SL₂ cusp frames, normalized by their actual Γ₀(N) widths. Trivial nebentypus makes each native cusp singular.",
    "The quotient test is the unit horocycle x∈[0,1], at every actual positive y, with the compact observation path transported by σ_h.",
    "Initial Re(s)>1 for the original primitive sum and the native absolutely convergent Dirichlet series. The continued pointwise assertion uses 1/2≤Re(s) and s≠1. At t=0 no denominator uses s−1/2.",
    "The initial residue coefficients, true Γ₀-admissible matrices, both unit-width frames, signed half-pairs, actual compact parameter disk and legal Cramer dilations are preserved."
  ],
  "removed_premises": [
    "Identified the native σ_h(observing) primitive Eisenstein series pointwise with its genuine diagonal and all earlier finite residue blocks at positive c. Right period is c w_h and both cusp widths enter the outgoing weight.",
    "Evaluated the complex zero-power Fourier integral by gamma continuation and paid absolute unit-segment integration against the previously summable original scatteringDirichletTerm values. The physical mean uses the full Gamma-normalized Dirichlet entry.",
    "Established differentiability of the actual compact observation integrals in the character completed family, and holomorphy of the q=1 completed integral off {0,1}, including its true regularized center.",
    "Transported mean regularity through the ordinary scalar, original adjugate/determinant and level denominators, all physical dilations and the inverse Young unit-character transform. Critical regularity includes every real t.",
    "Continued the independently calculated initial entry. Equality of physical native means at every y obtains by meromorphic identity and true value regularity; the y^(1−s) coefficient is common for all heights, including s=1/2."
  ],
  "remaining_full_premises": [
    "Full symmetric/unitary scattering matrix, functional equation of the whole native family, actual truncated Maass–Selberg/finite-part and residual constant channel, all-real continuous Plancherel/global normalized measure and completeness on the physical quotient.",
    "Complete normalized trace identity including exact geometric inversion for the manuscript R20 test function, holomorphic transforms/weight basis, all appropriate oldforms and actual native Hecke–Maass basis norms.",
    "Full ABL/Pascadi Theorem A plus J and regular/ordinary-large-sieve bounds on the exact coefficient families and common phase; original Kim–Sarnak bound/exceptional gap and the true 7/32 energy, zero-frequency corrections and final Eq24."
  ],
  "classification": "Classical analytic bridge and omitted formal machinery. Explicit genuine physical all-cusp constant term verified at source level; no substantive counterexample identified.",
  "independent_review": {
    "reviewer": "T10",
